# id: M67-minting-drops-the-node-tag
# covering-test: TestTwoNodesNeverMintTheSameTimestamp
# package: ./hlc/
# expect: killed
# power-seeds: 30
# power-detector: sweep
# power-measured: RULED to a sweep detector after the refutation pass refuted its opt-out (DESIGN-A6 section 43.4). The detector is ForeignTagStarts, and the previous declaration is the reason this class carries one: it opted out on the strength of IdentityCollisions, which fires about 1 in 660 -- 38 times in 25,000 seeds -- and concluded that an honest floor would need a sweep of thousands. Every number in that was right and the conclusion was not, because IdentityCollisions is not the only criterion that sees this class. ForeignTagStarts reads 589 in THIRTY seeds against a clean tree at zero, and not zero-at-thirty: the signed 25,000-seed exit run carries ForeignTagStarts = 0, which is why that criterion is asserted at exactly zero rather than floored. The margin here is in the MAGNITUDE rather than in the seed count -- 589 against 0 -- so 30 seeds is declared because 30 seeds is what was measured, and a larger count would be a number nobody took. This is M73's precedent: a class with no per-seed rate and an unambiguous sweep verdict declares the verdict. The fourth occurrence of DETECTOR-NOT-THE-CLASS (DESIGN-A6 section 43.4a), and the class that put the NO OTHER DETECTOR field into power-decl
# mutates: BUG-021's first half. The logical counter restarts at zero instead of at this node's slot, so two nodes over clocks a hold has pulled together mint the same (wall, logical). A transaction's start timestamp addresses the lock and the data version of every key it touches, so two transactions then share them: one commits, one is rolled back, and the version belongs to both
--- a/hlc/hlc.go
+++ b/hlc/hlc.go
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@
 	phys := Timestamp{Wall: c.phys.Wall()}
 	if c.last.Wall < phys.Wall {
 		// The physical clock has moved past everything this clock has issued, so
 		// the counter restarts -- at this node's slot, not at zero.
-		c.last = Timestamp{Wall: phys.Wall, Logical: c.id}
+		c.last = Timestamp{Wall: phys.Wall, Logical: 0}
 		return c.last
 	}
 	c.physRegressions++
